{
  "configuration_id": "config_049",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far shows config_037 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) at 0.706 acc is the best, with scvi_n200 providing a large jump over pca_n2000 (+4–7 pts) and imagenet_vit_l over resnet50 (+3 pts). However, the scgpt RNA encoder is completely untested across all 9 experiments, representing the largest remaining uncertainty in the design space. Config_049 (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) is a clean A/B test against config_037, differing only in the RNA encoder while holding all other parameters at their validated best settings. If scgpt outperforms scvi_n200, it opens a new promising direction; if it underperforms, it confirms scvi_n200 as the optimal encoder and lets us focus remaining budget on aggregation or fusion refinements. Under a limited budget, resolving this high-impact, zero-evidence dimension is more informative than testing a secondary variable (e.g., transformer aggregation) where prior evidence already favors avgpool."
}

